      "side": 1,
      "message": "@wtc@google.com, I think I might know where part of the confusion comes from.\n\nIn libaom, the `fixed_qp_offsets` array is deprecated. Currently, this array is NOT being used anywhere in the code. The array was first removed but then re-added (just the array, not the functionality) for ABI compat reasons with commit https://aomedia.googlesource.com/aom/+/010cd6c6.\n\nThis means the following comment in `encoder.h` is actually wrong:\n```\n  // If the value is 1, fixed QP offsets are either:\n  // - Given by the user, and stored in \u0027fixed_qp_offsets\u0027 array, OR\n  // - Picked automatically from cq_level.\r\n```\n\nOnly the second entry on the list is correct. This comment has been incorrect for a while -- I\u0027ll go fix it with a follow-up CL.\n\nThis means libaom\u0027s `use_fixed_qp_offsets \u003d 1` and SVT-AV1\u0027s `use-fixed-qindex-offsets \u003d 1` (with no qindex offset array values defined for SVT-AV1) differ only in the following way:\n- libaom: encoder applies a fixed QP scaling strategy for each frame type\n- SVT-AV1: encoder doesn\u0027t apply QP scaling, so encoder QP \u003d frame QP (i.e. the new functionality that `use_fixed_qp_offsets \u003d 2` introduces)\n\nDoes that make sense? The sentence in question is still correct.",
      "parentUuid": "9ab1f837_489cab9f",
